-- statement:
--   **The edge steps of the rational circuit are template-denoted**, uniformly in the modulus `N ∣ q ^ b` (`1 < N`), with templates independent of `q`, `b`, `N`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KIL5Tpl`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KIL.edgeSteps_toCircuit {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {W : ℕ} (C : QCircuit R m W) {q b N : ℕ}
--       (hq : q.Prime) (hN : N ∣ q ^ b) (hN1 : 1 < N) (X : IMat m)
--       (hg : GoodAtQ q ((C.den : ℚ)⁻¹ • ratM X)) :
--       AModel.edgeSteps (C.toCircuit (q ^ b)) N X = (edgeTplQ C X).map (TStep.eval N)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KIL5: the edge steps of the rational circuits are template-denoted*: `TStep m` is a step template: a shift template (`TSh`) or a field transposition.  The rational
--   circuit `QCircuit.toCircuit Q` (`AModelRat`) takes as Lemma 10 data of a frame change `X` the
--   integer lifts mod `Q` of the rational Bruhat factors `ratFacQ A` of `A = D⁻¹ • X`
--   (`facD Q D`).  Reduced mod `N ∣ Q`, these lifts are the reductions `redQ N` of the fixed
--   rationals, so every step of `edgeSteps` is the evaluation at `N` of a template whose unit is
--   `±|num|/den` and whose controls are `num/den` of fixed rationals.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** This lemma belongs to the item-language (IL) layer of the integer-multiplication-kappa campaign: tape-level programs (register programs over 64 item stacks of the `NLogN` multitape framework, definition bundles `IntMul_HvdH_M_Defs1`–`IntMul_HvdH_M_Defs8`) that implement the data-movement primitives of the OpenAI preprint *Integer multiplication below $n\log n$* (field moves, row split/merge, shifts, the uniform Proposition 11 interchange, Lemma 12 with fine $O(1)$-per-element costs, Gaussian record primitives, Proposition 14 pieces) with exact list denotations from the array-model bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*` and explicit cost bounds. All names refer to the definition bundles up to `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs18`.
